WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.726
[MUSIC]

00:00:10.726 --> 00:00:15.710
Change lives, change organizations,
change the world.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:21.280
The slogan of this school and a testament
to how much this university loves change.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.160
So much so they have to tell those, say
the word change three times in the same

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.480
slogan as you're going to forget
it's an important things.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.920
And in many ways we're all here because
we want to be those change agents.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.355
I know I do because I'm
a product of that change.

00:00:34.355 --> 00:00:38.230
Twenty years ago I was living
in broken homes, broken home.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.310
I couldn't eat everyday.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:40.940
I had terrible grades.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.260
An adult would tell me
things like college,

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.080
a career, standing on stage delivering
a speech are not for people like you.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.535
And to them I say look at me now.

00:00:52.535 --> 00:00:57.470
[APPLAUSE]
It

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:00.280
is amazing to be here,
to talk in front of all of you.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.340
I would never have dreamed it.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:05.540
To be someone who couldn't change
himself to someone who now change lives,

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.160
change organizations and change the world.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.820
And that's what I set out
to do in my first year.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.360
I wanted to bring what I thought was the
secret sauce to my success, my change, and

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.060
bring it places in the world
that didn't have it.

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.830
And so what I did was,
I said it was education.

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:22.610
I did my research,
I looked all around the world and

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:26.350
I found a place in northeast
India called West Bengal.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:30.512
Where the average income
of families is $600 a year,

00:01:30.512 --> 00:01:36.597
where nobody gets past the eighth grade,
and the average life expectancy is 32.

00:01:36.597 --> 00:01:38.199
32.

00:01:38.199 --> 00:01:40.520
And I said the biggest problem
they have is education.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.020
So I think I did what anyone would do.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.330
I bought a 50 seater bus.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.430
I tore it apart.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:50.520
I put a classroom inside of it and I drove
it into the jungles of west Bengal and

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:51.545
started to teach out of it.

00:01:51.545 --> 00:01:54.250
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; What they teach you in strategy, right?

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:57.390
And so, I want to first though,

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:01.550
before I start teaching, get
the permission of the village leadership.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:05.100
And so the pilot village I worked in,
Terpintar, there's a man named Collis.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.960
I explained to him what I was doing and
he said wait.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.600
Let me show you something.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.200
He took me outside of his house
to the center of the village.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.620
There was this bronze statue.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:19.040
And he said a villager made this because
this is what we are told education is.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.340
And it's that image that I think
is familiar to a lot of us,

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.480
it's the evolution of man.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.489
You know that image that we
all start out as primates.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.610
And we slowly evolved to upright man.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:31.310
Makes sense, right?

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:32.070
It's progress.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.960
Of course it's education.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.570
But the funny thing about what this
sculptor did in this village was he

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:37.250
added a step.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.060
To say where human kind was going.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.920
Where superior human beings were gonna be.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:47.400
And beyond upright man, it's hunched over,
typing away at a computer at a IT job.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.170
Right?
So why are you laughing.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.690
Like when was the last time you were in
a library looking at a guy making an Excel

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.250
sheet and was like yep,
evolved guy, right?

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.650
That's superior right there.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:01.630
And as much as it's funny, the thing about
this village is they're dead serious.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.070
And so Collis starts to explain to me,
this is what we're told.

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:07.440
IT is our salvation.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:12.160
And you're not the first person to
come and try and provide us education.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.150
In fact, so many have before, but they
always get it wrong because they never

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:19.800
answer the question,
what happens after the kids get educated?

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.520
Where do they go?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.760
Everyone is telling us IT is the solution,
but in a 50 kilometer radius around

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.690
this village, there's not
a single IT resource available.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:35.560
And so I asked him is there any cases, has
anybody made it before, and he said one.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.810
And I looked at that and
I know it's out of desperation and

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:42.430
sadness but I heard that as inspirational.

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.380
One well let's figure out what
this kid did, everything and

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.939
make sure everyone knows that and
then this problem will be solved.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.300
And so luckily his parents were
in this village of Tepantar and

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.750
I went to interview them.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.200
I said, what did your son do?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.840
I want to know everything.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:57.580
What did he study?

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.360
How did he study?

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:00.520
And his father looked at me,
he said, I don't know.

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:04.370
And not only that but he said,
I'm not supposed to know.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.510
Because my son is now in a better place.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:13.300
And I'm a craftsman and I'm proud of it
and that's what supported my family and

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:14.590
generations before me.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.140
But it doesn't make any money today and
people are telling us it doesn't.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:22.650
So anything I want to keep my son here,
to teach him my ways,

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.990
to teach him the heritage of my family.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.740
It's only going to hold him back.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:30.560
And so the best thing I can do for
him is let him go.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:37.510
When I heard that it hurt a lot and

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:40.290
I didn't understand why because
I didn't even know this kid.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.370
But what I do know is he's a role model,
he's what everyone should be.

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:47.120
He is smart, he is talented, he's driven.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:47.910
He made it.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:53.340
Everyone should be like him,
I couldn't figure it out,

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.400
until I realized that kid's me.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:04.590
Because, 30 years ago, I didn't grow up
in rural India, but my village was China.

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:09.260
And at that time my parents
wanted desperately to get out

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:12.070
because they went through a history
of terrible things happening.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.090
And they were lucky enough to be one
of the ones to set foot in America and

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.210
start a new.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.480
In the land of prosperity.

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:22.400
And the first thing they wanted was
they wanted to give birth to a child so

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:23.750
he could live up in this prosperity.

00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:24.300
And that was me.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:30.600
But shortly after I was born they had to
go back to China for a variety of reasons.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.700
And so they were left with the tough
decision of either keeping the family

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:39.880
together but take me back to a country
that will forever limit my potential, or

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:45.550
to keep me with unlimited potential but
to rip away the family and

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:49.080
just like that family in Tepantar,
my parents chose prosperity.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.100
As much as it hurts to not be around them,
to never know if you're gonna see them

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.710
again in some ways they were
right in that decision.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.190
Right, I'm standing here.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.090
When I said look at me
now everyone applauded.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:07.650
That I can be this person who changes
lives, changes organizations and

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.410
changes the world.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:13.520
But to get there I had to change
my friends, change my family, and

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.670
change my home over and over again.

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:18.470
And be proud of it because that's change.

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.040
Now imagine if that were
the slogan of this school.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:27.765
Stanford University change your friends,
change your family, change your home.

00:06:27.765 --> 00:06:30.230
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Great.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.810
I mean I didn't get the best
grades in marketing but

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:34.025
I can tell you not inspirational right?

00:06:34.025 --> 00:06:36.800
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; But that's what happened.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:40.590
And I don't say that because I want
to change the slogan of the school.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:42.470
It's done wonders, it's an amazing slogan.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.870
But, what I do propose is a slogan for
our lives.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:49.390
Especially as we leave the school and
get out there to pursue our careers.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:54.450
To not always be so obsessed with change,
to be disruptive, but

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.020
to take on the challenge
of simply to keep,

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.430
to keep your friends,
to keep your family, to keep your home.

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:10.335
Thank you.
[APPLAUSE]

00:07:10.335 --> 00:07:15.385
[MUSIC]

